functions can be created freely with the func keyword a name and any  number of parameters. This then registeres that function for autocomplete, even in other scripts that reference the type the funciton is used in.

syntax is
func func_name(parameter_type param) : return_type
{
   code;
}

if no return type is specified you can still return whatever you want it just isnt required.

functions can be abstract and if they are they MUST be overriden in any inherited classes and cannot be called until they are,

overidden functions are called like this.
this.base.function_name();

you override a function by simply creating one with the same name but without the abstract keyword.
